Subject: [PATCH] 1454 and 3466: any form of the plan verb counts; a tapped
 button's own text is a pick
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Box 53065.
- 1454 run 1: „მინდა ბახვას ასისტენტს დაველაპარაკო და შევეცადო, …" — the
  plan-sentence pattern knew only „დაველაპარაკები", so the reply counted as
  having none, the server's sentence was added, and the reply carried two.
  Every form of the verb now counts, so the second is dropped.
- 3466 pair 4: the buttons did not carry the name („სანტექნიკის ნომერი",
  „საბურთალოს სანტექნიკის ნომერი"), and the helper tapped the first. A
  tapped button's own text is now read as its position, like „მეორე"; when
  no button starts with the name, the namesake buttons are those that use
  words the search showed about them. The phone still goes only when the
  buttons settle it; otherwise the run's own choice stands.

What this does not reach: in pair 4 the run never called the share tool and
asked again instead; a server-settled tap would need a new confirmation line
for the helper (Misho's text).

